(The independent review set identified these important alignment items:) Tj
0.12 0.16 0.22 rg
/F1 8.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 42.0 415.0 Tm
(1. The hardware reference requires power button GPIO4, but the current firmware configuration) Tj
0.12 0.16 0.22 rg
/F1 8.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 42.0 402.0 Tm
(and main loop do not yet implement GPIO4 shutdown/wake behavior.) Tj
0.12 0.16 0.22 rg
/F1 8.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 42.0 389.0 Tm
(2. The hardware reference assigns MPU INT GPIO16 and static straps; the current firmware only) Tj
0.12 0.16 0.22 rg
/F1 8.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 42.0 376.0 Tm
(initializes I2C and does not yet provide a qualified MPU driver.) Tj
0.12 0.16 0.22 rg
/F1 8.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 42.0 363.0 Tm
(3. TFT/touch GPIO constants exist, but a complete runtime display/touch driver and CS) Tj
0.12 0.16 0.22 rg
/F1 8.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 42.0 350.0 Tm
(transaction arbitration are not yet proven by hardware tests.) Tj
0.12 0.16 0.22 rg
/F1 8.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 42.0 337.0 Tm
(4. The current firmware defaults SD CS and modem PWRKEY to -1, which is the safe choice until) Tj
0.12 0.16 0.22 rg
/F1 8.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 42.0 324.0 Tm
(those connections are physically qualified.) Tj
0.12 0.16 0.22 rg
/F1 8.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 42.0 311.0 Tm
(5. GPIO21 software polarity is active-low correct, but the reference's hi-Z rail-off behavior) Tj
0.12 0.16 0.22 rg
/F1 8.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 42.0 298.0 Tm
(and reset/deep-sleep sequence still require board-level validation.) Tj
0.12 0.16 0.22 rg
/F1 8.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 42.0 285.0 Tm
(6. Current and capacitor values in this document are estimates from the supplied reference, not) Tj
0.12 0.16 0.22 rg
/F1 8.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 42.0 272.0 Tm
(certification for the actual ESP32 board revision or breakout modules.) Tj
